<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's PPC backs new E. Cape port bid.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's PPC backs new E. Cape port bid.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African cement firm Pretoria Portland Cement Ltd (PPC) said on Tuesday it was backing a multi-billion rand initiative for a new industrial port in the Eastern Cape region.</p>
<p>PPC said it was donating 50,000 rand to a fund set up by the region's Chamber of Commerce to help campaign for the port, which could generate an estimated five billion rand in investment and directly create 3,000 jobs and indirectly support 45,000 more.</p>
<p>The bid is being put forward by the Eastern Cape cities of Port Elizabeth and Uitenhage.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
